                <pb facs="0964" n="844" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg844"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Schuyler to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Bangkok,
                                Siam</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1905-08-10"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">August 10,
                    1905</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(With reference to the boycott of American goods, Chargé Schuyler reports that
                    3,000 Bangkok Chinese at a meeting held here have telegraphed to their agents at
                    Singapore and Hongkong not to ship any more American goods to Siam.)</p>
            </div>
